# Compile-probe manifest — drives `make check-metal-compiles` for this crate.
# Same format and same gate as the KV-codec manifest at
# crates/rmlx-kv-quant/src/metal/probes/kernels.manifest; see the README there
# for the probe layout.
#
# Format:  <body.metal> | <header or -> | <name:type,...> | [NAME=VALUE,...]
#   type: u = uint buffer, f = float buffer
#
# Every `.metal` file in the parent directory must appear here, as a body or as
# a `../`-prefixed header. The gate fails on one that does not.

# The language-version probe. This is the one body in the tree guarded by
# `#if __HAVE_TENSOR__`, so it is what gives the gate's metal4.0 pass something
# real to check: at metal3.0 the guard is inactive and the body compiles to
# nothing, at metal4.0 the descriptor must instantiate.
nax_probe.metal | ../nax_probe_header.metal | out:f
